# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefill-3 window (the masked tail pass of a prompt as a trace replay; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefill-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-pf3-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-pf3-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a NEW tag in every template (a rebuild under an existing tag keeps the old image). This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a smoke job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the same
# in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix steps (AP1, R1, R2) do not forward the selection into their container and serve the base checkpoint: a tail pass
# replays the same traces on either.
# A2 (EXACTNESS of the traced tail, buckets 256 and 512, STOP): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-pf3-s5-audit-mid, the same twin for the other two programs
# (bucket 256 is the stock SDPA at two q chunks a head; 512 is the one-q-per-core call). Tests: warmup,coding,parked_turns,concurrent8_steady,agent_turns. READ as A1: every
# audit line exact=True, a bucket-256 and a bucket-512 line at least twice each, no mismatch, no fall-back. ANY failure is NO-GO for that bucket (the BUCKETS knob drops it)
# and halts the window. the lines in the container log: "[PINDIAG] lever N route installed: ... tailtrace=traced audit" once; on the arms "[PINDIAG] prefill tail trace
# engaged buckets=.. traces=<n> sink=<id> taps=5,19,33,47,61 arena_mb=<mb> arena_address=.. freed=<k> uncovered=0 capture_ms=.." once and one "[PF3] tail mode=traced
# bucket=.. valid=.. start=.. ms=.. stage_ms=.. replay_ms=.." per traced tail pass; on the control one "[PF3] tail mode=eager bucket=.. valid=.. start=.. ms=.." per tail
# pass below the 2,048-row bucket and no "engaged" line; no "fell back" line, no "[PF3] tail skip" line that the control would not also take (a skip is a call that ran the
# stock pass: vision, an untraced bucket, another page-table width, another tap set) and no program growth after the warm anywhere MEMORY READ (the ledger is on in these
# profiles): "[MEMLEDGER] phase=P7 ... trace_used=.." per chip after the attach is the trace region the lever's traces took (against the control's P7 line: python3 -B
# scripts/ci/pf3_report.py --control <control log> --arm <this log>, or --headroom <log> for the fit of N traces), and the P7 DRAM line is what the arena holds (the arena
# is 320 MB a chip at its default; the admission need of a prompt of 2,048 tokens or more is unchanged, so a "dram admission hold" that the control did not draw is the
# arena's) CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)" once, a "weight cache ...:
# found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models answer names
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED. Duration (estimate): 80 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-pf3-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-pf3-s5-audit-mid
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,parked_turns,concurrent8_steady,agent_turns
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=135
